  "coverage_interpretation": "338 numeric evidence records. 77 of 136 source identities have size references, leaving 59 numeric size-reference gaps. Murphy gains a source-selected height-signal meridional span, not a measured whole-eddy diameter, and a selected peak dynamic-topography diagnostic, not physical eddy depth. Fourteen identities have structure diagnostics; sixteen entries lack their own numeric evidence.",
  "scope_limits": [
    "Original JHUAPL institutional PDF acquired and Figure 4 visually reviewed. Original source assets remain in ignored cache, not republished.",
    "Murphy is the named Gulf case dated 20 June 1988, not the unrelated East Australian Current Murphy of 2015. Registry physical identity association remains unverified.",
    "Two manually isolated bracketing crossings, OSW-chosen 0.30 m level and 0.25/0.35 m sensitivity describe a selected profile signal, not an author-defined eddy edge or continuously above-level interval. No local troughs or missing ink filled.",
    "Latitude-axis conversion yields a meridional projection only; unknown longitude/track obliquity prevents along-track distance, radius or diameter inference.",
    "Selected main-lobe peak is dynamic topography relative to the source mean-height reference, not eddy depth or total vertical extent.",
    "Separate AXBT comparison is several days apart. Its cited 4 cm agreement is not assigned as width uncertainty; schematic inset circle is not a measured boundary.",
    "Six-pixel reading allowance, two-pixel independent anchor shifts, ink gates and outward rounding express reading/operator sensitivity, not a confidence interval or physical instrument/product errors.",
    "No physical footprint, state containment, seasonal playback, runtime or release installation."
  ],
